.TITLE "homebrew"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Homebrew is a tool that lets you **install software** directly from your terminal.

It was created by __Max Howell__ in __2009__.
You can think of it like an App Store for the command line.
It manages the **downloading and setup** of tools so you can start using them right away.

.DIV "EXAMPLE"
brew install wget

.DIV "EXPLANATION"
**brew install** finds and adds a new tool to your computer.

Here, __brew__ is the name of the tool.
__install__ is the action that gets the software.
__wget__ is an example of a tool you might want to get.

This is much faster than searching the web for a download button.

.DIV "EXAMPLE"
brew update

.DIV "EXPLANATION"
**brew update** makes sure Homebrew knows about the newest versions of software.

Here, __update__ tells the tool to **check for any changes** or new tools available online.

Think of this like **checking the news** to see what has been updated since you last looked.

.DIV "EXAMPLE"
brew list

.DIV "EXPLANATION"
**brew list** shows you everything you have installed using Homebrew.

Here, __list__ is the subcommand that **shows your collection**.

Use this when you want to **see what you already have** or if you forgot the name of a tool.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Homebrew keeps your tools organized and easy to manage.
Make it a habit to run **brew update** before you **install something new** so you always have the latest version.
